---
import retrospectiveMarkdown from "../../../docs/RETROSPECTIVE.md?raw";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { parseInstrumentFailures } from "../lib/docs";
import { formatDate, RUN_NOTES, RUNS, stageByName } from "../lib/fixtures";
import { inlineMarkdown } from "../lib/markdown";
import { docUrl } from "../lib/site";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const failures = parseInstrumentFailures(retrospectiveMarkdown);

const runs = RUNS.map((run) => ({
  run,
  note: RUN_NOTES[run.slug]!.text,
  retrieved: stageByName(run, "retrieve")?.n_out ?? 0,
  // The gate stage's OUTPUT, not "papers licensed": on a run where two papers collapsed to one
  // id the two differ by the collapse (DEF-0007 records this exact mislabel in relevance_screen.py).
  licensed: stageByName(run, "licence_gate")?.n_out ?? 0,
  clusters: run.clusters.length,
}));
---

<Base
  title="BioLit Copilot: evidence viewer"
  description="Four real runs of a biomedical literature pipeline, shown stage by stage, with what each stage dropped and why."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="intro">
      <h1>Four questions, followed through every stage that answered them</h1>
      <div class="prose lede">
        <p>
          BioLit Copilot answers clinical questions from the biomedical literature: it retrieves
          papers, links what they mention to MeSH, refuses anything its licence does not allow it
          to quote, clusters what co-occurs, and writes a deterministic answer.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each page below is one real run, recorded when it happened. The point of showing them is
          the accounting: every stage says what it took in, what it removed and why, and what it
          left out on purpose.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="runs-h">
      <h2 id="runs-h" class="visually-quiet">The runs</h2>
      <ul class="runs">
        {
          runs.map(({ run, note, retrieved, licensed, clusters }) => (
            <li class="run">
              <a class="query" href={`${base}runs/${run.slug}/`}>
                “{run.query}”
              </a>
              <p class="funnel num">
                <span>
                  <strong>{retrieved}</strong> retrieved
                </span>
                <span>
                  <strong>{licensed}</strong> past the licence gate
                </span>
                <span>
                  <strong>{clusters}</strong> {clusters === 1 ? "cluster" : "clusters"} in the answer
                </span>
              </p>
              <p class="note">{note}</p>
              <p class="date">Retrieved {formatDate(run.generated_at)}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section failures" aria-labelledby="failures-h">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="failures-h">{failures.heading}</h2>
        <p>
          The project's retrospective argues that its most durable results are the times the
          measurement itself failed. Quoted from <a href={docUrl("RETROSPECTIVE.md")}>RETROSPECTIVE.md</a>,
          section 4. None of these is a property of the four runs above; they are about how the
          project was evaluated.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="failure-list">
        {
          failures.items.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
              <p set:html={inlineMarkdown(item.body)} />
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-top: 4rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    max-width: 20ch;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .visually-quiet {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
  }
  .runs {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .run {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.4rem 2.5rem;
    padding: 1.6rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .query {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 1 / span 2;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .query:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--eosin);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }
  .funnel {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.2rem 1.2rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }
  .funnel strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .note {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }
  .date {
    grid-column: 1;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .failure-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 2rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.6rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .failure-list li::marker {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .failure-list h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
  .failure-list p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .run {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .query,
    .date {
      grid-row: auto;
      grid-column: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
